turboexl3_ling builds against the mlx-serve plugin kit and turboexl3 (build.zig.zon, by URL and hash). It vendors
nothing: the code below came from mlx-serve, which no longer carries it, and is maintained here (no copy to sync).

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
mlx-serve
https://github.com/ddalcu/mlx-serve
Copyright (c) 2026 David Dalcu
Licensed under the MIT License.

src/streamed/ is mlx-serve's expert streamer as it stood at ddalcu/mlx-serve bc6c5f2c (its src/sdk/weights/streamed/,
with the EXL3 lane's types from src/sdk/quant/exl3/stream/ in src/streamed/exl3lane/), before mlx-serve replaced it with
the kit's generic stream (#1131): the files Ling's bank source reaches, with this plugin's edits (Ling's stream seams,
the imports pointed at this plugin's files, the module-owned arch SDK and the tests left out; each file's first line
names its mlx-serve path). src/streamed/ling_source.zig, src/ling_*.zig, src/bank_rows.zig and src/clamps.zig are this
plugin's own code. src/host/{env,log,shared}.zig and src/host_shims.zig are this plugin's code standing in for
mlx-serve's registry, log, unit globals and C++ shims over MLX's private headers.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
mlx-stream
https://github.com/davidtai/mlx-stream
Copyright (c) 2026 David Tai
Licensed under the MIT License.

mlx-serve absorbed mlx-stream (the SSD expert streamer, its SDK and C read pool); src/streamed/ holds the parts Ling's
bank reads. The packed expert record and manifest formats and the streamed-bank layout are David Tai's earlier work.
ExLlamaV3 (https://github.com/turboderp-org/exllamav3, Copyright (c) turboderp, MIT): the EXL3 format the bank reads
follows exllamav3; no exllamav3 code is shipped.

